\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jesu! the very thought is sweet,
\par In that dear name all heart-joys meet;
\par But sweeter than the honey far
\par The glimpses of His presence are.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. No word is sung more sweet than this,
\par No name is heard more full of bliss,
\par No thought brings sweeter comfort nigh
\par Than Jesus, Son of God most high.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I seek for Jesus in repose,
\par When round my heart its chambers close;
\par Abroad, and when I shut the door,
\par I long for Jesus evermore.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. With Mary in the morning gloom
\par I seek for Jesus at the tomb;
\par For Him, with love's most earnest cry,
\par I seek with heart and not with eye.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Jesus, to God the Father gone,
\par Is seated on the heavenly throne:
\par My heart hath also passed from me,
\par That where He is there it may  be.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. We follow Jesus now, and praise
\par The voice of prayer, the hymn of praise
\par That He at last may make us meet
\par With Him to gain the heavenly seat.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

